{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Is it not so, if you do well.</b> Its meaning is as its Targum renders." "<b>Sin crouches at the opening.</b> At the opening of your grave your sin is stored up." "<b>And its desire is toward you.</b> That of sin — it is the evil inclination, always craving and yearning to make you stumble." "<b>And you shall rule over it.</b> If you wish, you can overcome it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:29.317507096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}